<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:11Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Germany's Merz visits Kyiv as Russia strikes bridge</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2c19a5c2824a2a6dd011ec84e776e7c2e7c8851f866999704f2feec96058b5bd</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T14:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-merz-visits-kyiv-as-russia-strikes-bridge/a-79534734--9ac3ff548705.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-merz-visits-kyiv-as-russia-strikes-bridge/a-79534734?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As air raid sirens sounded in Kyiv, Chancellor Merz called on President Putin to end his "senseless war" and announced new measures to support Ukraine, including plans for joint Ukrainian-German drone production.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Many believe Merkel more capable than Merz</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d2d687f655a34a034afb0d4f304180c0a58b9dc62d91f71e64dc6dbb24e614c0</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T08:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-many-believe-merkel-more-capable-than-merz/live-79528092--f23ed5eb8e52.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-many-believe-merkel-more-capable-than-merz/live-79528092?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nearly half of Germans view former Chancellor Angela Merkel as better suited to handle Germany's challenges than current Chancellor Friedrich Merz. Also, today is the last day of Oktoberfest in Munich. DW has the latest.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>German reunification: How inequality is shaping a new East German identity</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c4cc0990f35cee2556df1d65431f2c1e055bb0f3241e24fb34f620a4fb22d68f</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T04:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-reunification-how-inequality-is-shaping-a-new-east-german-identity/a-79518541--28106a765624.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-reunification-how-inequality-is-shaping-a-new-east-german-identity/a-79518541?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new study highlights persistent structural disparities in wealth and leadership positions between East and West Germany, 36 years after reunification.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>ARD-Deutschlandtrend survey: Germans unite in frustration over the government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:507b83aa7e0e9d3c4eb1259cc623e0b16fbcfbd1baf6dfef7c8bc7b8b5901737</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T11:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ard-deutschlandtrend-survey-germans-unite-in-frustration-over-the-government/a-79515172--1741214668c0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ard-deutschlandtrend-survey-germans-unite-in-frustration-over-the-government/a-79515172?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">On the 36th anniversary of reunification, Germans are dissatisfied with the country's political leaders. They don't believe they'll be able to handle the challenges posed by AI, Russia and Donald Trump.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Klopp wins first game as Germany coach, without 'top dogs'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d68e616aab0f56ae957eb5071994a0b7620bd99d6c4774bc4f627b64b1f9ffb8</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T22:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/klopp-wins-first-game-as-germany-coach-without-top-dogs/a-79508898--6c1fca750e8a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/klopp-wins-first-game-as-germany-coach-without-top-dogs/a-79508898?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">It may have taken a little longer than he would have liked, but Jürgen Klopp has finally won a game as Germany coach. Despite a number of debutants, it was a familiar face who stood out in the victory over Serbia.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Servers at Munich's iconic Oktoberfest call for more respect</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9eb74ecf285f2b33fdc418ead1d33e89c82615450c63b0536f03f141569f9248</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T13:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/servers-at-munich-s-iconic-oktoberfest-call-for-more-respect/a-79491207--cd91ce591124.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/servers-at-munich-s-iconic-oktoberfest-call-for-more-respect/a-79491207?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Oktoberfest is famous the world over for beer, brass band music and Bavarian traditions. But staff are also reporting incidents of racism and sexism, and are taking a stand against discrimination.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Three-way battle for power in world chess: Who will be elected FIDE president in Samarkand?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:41465734b777a0c6b6cf12bfbbc18b0f3bd2fe4b340f6c4eab9c5fbe099e667e</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T18:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301--bc60333e85fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The era of Russian presidents is coming to an end at the World Chess Federation (FIDE). Two Germans and one Kazakh are up for election. Among the issues at play are money, Kremlin influence, and unanswered questions.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
